        <mxCell id="card-legend-notes" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Large dashed frame: infra perimeter · small: functional group&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;⚠ Gx&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: docs and code disagree, see &quot;Gaps&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1630" width="560" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-steps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#34d399&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Request path · a callback of the import workflow&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; The CMP dispatches import.yml on main with the CNP-Portal installation token, then polls the run status. &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; An ephemeral runner takes the job.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; The job asks GitHub for an ID token with audience cmp-import, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; and calls https://cmp.3istor.com/api/import/worker/* with it, User-Agent cnp-import-worker/1: Cloudflare refuses urllib&amp;#39;s default one (error 1010).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; Relayed through the platform tunnel, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt; then Envoy matches HTTPRoute cmp-api-import-worker, whose SecurityPolicy checks the GitHub signature and the audience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;7&lt;/span&gt; The CMP checks the claims again: repository and owner ids, workflow ref on main, job_workflow_sha in IMPORT_WORKFLOW_SHAS, workflow_dispatch, run id and attempt, runner_environment self-hosted.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt; For each app with a secret, the CMP writes the Kubernetes auth role &amp;lt;project&amp;gt;-&amp;lt;app&amp;gt;-role (policy project-&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;-read-policy, mount kubernetes on-prem, kubernetes-&amp;lt;cloud&amp;gt; otherwise), &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt; the secrets under project-&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;app&amp;gt;/imports, &lt;span style=&quot;background-color:#f8fafc;color:#020617;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 4px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; then one registry commit with the digests.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="1260" width="1000" height="420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-bg" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#a78bfa&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; Envoy fetches the GitHub Actions JWKS. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; The CMP caches it for 1 h, refetches on an unknown key id at most once a minute, and keeps the cached keys when GitHub is unreachable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #f8fafc;color:#f8fafc;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD picks the new record up and syncs the apps.&lt;br&gt;• Deleting an imported app deletes its Vault role. The chart (infra-templates#26) refuses any vaultPath outside project-&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;app&amp;gt; and any vaultRole other than &amp;lt;project&amp;gt;-&amp;lt;app&amp;gt;-role.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1720" y="1260" width="1180" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-ops" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb7185&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Operating rule: allow each analyzer commit&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• The workflow runs at the head of main of extern-project-analyzer, so &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;every commit merged on main&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; changes job_workflow_sha, even one that leaves import.yml alone.&lt;br&gt;• Until its full SHA is in IMPORT_WORKFLOW_SHAS (K3s arcl-cmp/cmp-values.yaml), every callback gets 401 and imports fail. Merge the analyzer PR, then the K3s PR that adds the SHA.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1720" y="1490" width="1180" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps between docs and code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Transport.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; TLS ends at Cloudflare. In-cluster hops are plain HTTP, Vault included (tls_disable).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G4&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Coupling.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Tunnels target Envoy&amp;#39;s Service by name.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#fb923c&quot;&gt;G6&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#f8fafc&quot;&gt;Token call.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; No cluster-local path to auth.3istor.com found: likely hairpins via Cloudflare. Not used by this route.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#0b1222;strokeColor=#1e293b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#e2e8f0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="640" width="800" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
